## Cross-check (Section 6.3 requirement)

For V=10 and V=100, Bellman-Ford was run from every vertex as source and
compared against the corresponding row of Floyd-Warshall's output on the
exact same graph (`./cross_check tests/bf_gen/bf_10.txt` /
`bf_100.txt`):

| Graph | Sources checked | Result |
|---|---|---|
| bf_10.txt (V=10) | 10/10 | **ALL SOURCES MATCH** |
| bf_100.txt (V=100) | 100/100 | **ALL SOURCES MATCH** |

## Notes 

- All times are single-run wall-clock measurements from
  `std::chrono::high_resolution_clock`; the smallest cases are
  noise-dominated (sub-microsecond), reported as-is per the spec's guidance
  on very fast inputs.
- Test-data generation seeds are fixed (`std::mt19937 rng(123)` for
  Bellman-Ford, `rng(456)` for Floyd-Warshall), so re-running the generator
  tools reproduces the exact files these results were measured on.
